.TH RSH 1 "" "" "mcos Manual"
.SH NAME
rsh \- run a command or a shell on another computer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rsh
.RB [ \-n ]
.I host
.RI [ command ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rsh
connects to
.BR rshd (1)
on another computer, over its network cards (TCP, port 514).
.I host
is the other computer's name (its
.BR hostname (1)),
or its network card id
.RB ( "lsdev \-i"
shows it), whole, or as much of its start as names one computer that
answers (rsh asks every rshd in reach, and each answers with its name); a
.B *
at its end is allowed. A name said in full wins over an id's start. It asks
up to three times before a host is unknown (as ARP does: a busy computer may
miss one), so an unknown host takes a moment.
.PP
With a
.I command
(its words joined by spaces), the other computer's
.B sh \-c
runs it. Its input is rsh's (none with
.BR \-n ),
its output and errors are rsh's, apart, and
.B rsh
ends as it did: its exit status, or 128 and the signal's number if a
signal ended it.
.PP
With no command, a login: a shell on a pty on the other computer, as big
as this terminal. This terminal goes raw, so every key goes there as it's
typed, ^C and the arrows included; a change of this terminal's size
(SIGWINCH) goes there too.
.B ~.
at the start of a line disconnects, and
.B ~~
sends one
.BR ~ .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
No input for the command (as from
.BR /dev/null ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
The command's, or the shell's; 1 when the host isn't found, the
connection fails, or it's lost.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rsh 1b9c0e uptime
rsh 1b9c0e
cat notes | rsh 1b9c0e 'cat > /notes'
.fi
.SH NOTES
Berkeley's r\-commands are its model: no passwords and no encryption
(anyone whose card reaches the other computer's can do this), which is
why their names were kept, and not ssh's. BSD's rsh sent errors on a
second connection, never told how the command ended, and ran rlogin when
given no command; this one sends everything on one connection, framed, ends
as the command did, and logs in itself. It speaks only to mcos's rshd.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rshd (1),
.BR rcp (1),
.BR rc (1)
